    "note": "candidate-003 — fixed the broken seams + t=0 visibility. The seams (and the at-t=0 invisibility in the render hero) came from the SLIVER SWEEP: each segment was subdivided into ~36 radial slivers that faded in over time — so early frames showed radial seams and a partial ring. Replaced with SOLID FULL SECTORS: one tight-masked tile per segment, painted at full alpha from frame 0. Now the whole donut is visible at t=0 (the render hero shows the entire layout at once) and each segment is seamless — the only separators are the intentional 2° gaps between segments. The center value still counts up ($0 → $12,480). I verified by rendering + extracting frame 0. (Provenance: candidate-002.mosaic was frozen before this change; this candidate's .mosaic is frozen too.)",
